[00:08.61]A: I used to rule the world
[00:12.30]B: Seas would rise when I gave the word
[00:14.78]A: Now in the morning, I sleep alone
[00:19.10]B: Sweep the streets I used to own
[00:36.09]A: I used to roll the dice
[00:40.15]B: Feel the fear in my enemy's eyes
[00:43.41]A: Listened as the crowd would sing
[00:47.22]AB: "Now the old king is dead, long live the king"
[00:50.06]A: One minute I held the key
[00:54.03]B: Next, the walls were closed on me
[00:56.70]A: And I discovered that my castles stand
[01:00.96]B: Upon pillars of salt and pillars of sand
[01:04.78]AB: I hear Jerusalem bells a-ringing
[01:08.66]AB: Roman cavalry choirs are singing
[01:12.12]AB: Be my mirror, my sword and shield
[01:15.24]AB: My missionaries in a foreign field
[01:19.04]A: For some reason, I can't explain
[01:22.44]B: Once you'd gone, there was never
[01:25.07]A: Never an honest word
[01:28.78]AB: And that was when I ruled the world
[01:45.43]A: It was a wicked and wild wind
[01:49.60]B: Blew down the doors to let me in
[01:52.29]A: Shattered windows and the sound of drums
[01:56.65]B: People couldn't believe what I'd become
[01:59.84]A: Revolutionaries wait
[02:03.68]B: For my head on a silver plate
[02:06.13]A: Just a puppet on a lonely string
[02:10.70]B: Oh, who would ever want to be king?
[02:14.47]AB: I hear Jerusalem bells a-ringing
[02:18.07]AB: Roman cavalry choirs are singing
[02:21.48]AB: Be my mirror, my sword and shield
[02:24.94]AB: My missionaries in a foreign field
[02:28.42]A: For some reason, I can't explain
[02:32.00]B: I know Saint Peter won't call my name
[02:35.19]A: Never an honest word
[02:38.26]AB: But that was when I ruled the world
[03:10.60]AB: Hear Jerusalem bells a-ringing
[03:13.65]AB: Roman cavalry choirs are singing
[03:17.23]AB: Be my mirror, my sword and shield
[03:20.51]AB: My missionaries in a foreign field
[03:24.13]A: For some reason, I can't explain
[03:27.59]B: I know Saint Peter won't call my name
[03:30.73]A: Never an honest word
[03:33.97]AB: But that was when I ruled the world
